From 627d6914e730307d1de9d6e65a1bc702e42e1e67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:11:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Retain client upgrade recovery across deferred
 bundle swaps

Why: checkout/backend updates and Desktop bundle installation run on separate clocks. Existing skew and lag mitigation preserves idle and turn gates, but a refused legacy edit only produced a transient reminder whose update action could target a remote backend.

Keep one client-install-wide acknowledgement bit and a coalesced persistent recovery notice. Rehydrate after reload; explicitly open client Updates on click. Do not replay edits, apply updates, restart busy sessions or alter archive intent.

Proof: 3 baseline notification failures; 9 recovery tests green; 8/8 notification mutants killed. Real POSIX mac_swap copy and install failures retain advanced Git code and the complete old bundle with warnings. Existing legacy HTTP refusal and seven-boundary interrupted-swap tests pass. 82 consumer files: 81 pass, one fixture teardown needed explicit dismissal; affected file rerun green. TypeScript and scripts/check pass. External state skew/defer composition: 4 pass; bundle-lag suite passes. Native signed Mac installation not claimed; the earlier incident cause remains undetermined.
